  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "This cultivar comes alive in the fall with its vivid scarlet color. The small leaves are deeply divided into five ovate lobes with tail-like tips. The margins are distinctly toothed. The red leafstalks are stiff and slender. 'Tobiosho' grows into an upright, wide-topped medium-sized tree. It was named after the Oretended gon nurseryman who selected it. with tube."
